@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptions<GiftOfTheGivers.Services.OrganisationOptions> OrganisationOptions
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Notice";
    var organisation = OrganisationOptions.Value;
    var privacyContact = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(organisation.InformationOfficerEmail)
        ? organisation.ContactEmail
        : organisation.InformationOfficerEmail;
}

<div class="container my-5">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-9 mx-auto">
            <h1 class="display-5 mb-3">Privacy Notice</h1>
            <p class="lead">How @organisation.Name collects, uses and protects your personal information under the
                Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013 (POPIA).</p>

            <div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
                <strong>Draft for legal review.</strong> This notice describes what the software actually does. The
                organisation must confirm the retention periods, Information Officer and lawful bases with its legal
                advisers before the site handles real personal information.
            </div>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-5">1. Who is responsible</h2>
            <p>@organisation.Name is the responsible party for the personal information processed on this site.
                Privacy requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:@privacyContact">@privacyContact</a>.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-5">2. What we collect and why</h2>
            <div class="table-responsive">
                <table class="table table-bordered align-middle small">
                    <thead class="table-light">
                        <tr><th scope="col">When you…</th><th scope="col">We collect</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Donate</td>
                            <td>Name, email, amount, currency, project, optional message, payment reference</td>
                            <td>To process and confirm your payment, issue receipts and donation certificates, and keep financial records</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Apply to volunteer</td>
                            <td>Name, email, optional phone, city, skills, availability; optionally date of birth and an emergency contact</td>
                            <td>To assess your application, contact you and coordinate deployments safely</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Contact us</td>
                            <td>Name, email, subject and message</td>
                            <td>To reply to you</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Register an account</td>
                            <td>Name, email, password (stored only as a salted hash)</td>
                            <td>To let you sign in and see your donation history</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p>We ask for your consent on each form. You can withdraw consent at any time by contacting us; this does not
                affect records we must keep by law (for example donation records for tax purposes).</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-5">3. Who we share it with</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>PayFast</strong> processes card and EFT payments. We never receive or store your card details.</li>
                <li><strong>SendGrid</strong> (when enabled) delivers confirmation emails.</li>
                <li><strong>Microsoft Azure</strong> hosts the application and database.</li>
                <li><strong>Google Fonts and jsDelivr</strong> serve fonts and icons, which means your browser contacts them when pages load.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Authorised staff of the organisation can see donation, volunteer and inquiry records. Staff access is
                granted individually and every access-level change is recorded in an audit log.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-5">4. How long we keep it</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Donation records: as long as tax law requires (proposed: 5 years after the end of the tax year).</li>
                <li>Volunteer applications: while you volunteer with us, and up to 2 years after your last activity (proposed).</li>
                <li>Contact inquiries: up to 1 year after the inquiry is handled (proposed).</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-5">5. Your rights</h2>
            <p>Under POPIA you may ask to access, correct or delete your personal information, object to processing, and
                lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator (South Africa). Account holders can download or delete
                their account data from <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Manage/PersonalData">Manage account → Personal data</a>.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-5">6. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Sign-in cookie</strong> — keeps you signed in (essential).</li>
                <li><strong>Anti-forgery cookie</strong> — protects forms against cross-site request forgery (essential).</li>
                <li><strong>Temporary message cookie</strong> — shows one-off confirmation messages (essential).</li>
                <li><strong>Session storage</strong> — remembers that you have seen the intro animation for this browser session.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We do not use advertising or analytics cookies.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-5">7. Security</h2>
            <p>Data is sent over HTTPS, passwords are hashed, staff pages require the Employee role, and payment
                confirmations are verified with PayFast before they are recorded.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
